`/api/generate-seo` extracted `ytChannel`, `fbAccount`, and `ttAccount` from the request payload but silently dropped them — `brandContext` was built from `folderName` only, so the AI never received channel identity when generating SEO via this endpoint.

## Change

Replaced the single-field `brandContext` assignment with the same multi-part builder already used in `/api/generate-premium-seo`:

```js
// Before
const brandContext = folderName ? `Brand/Channel: ${folderName}. ` : "";

// After
const brandParts = [];
if (folderName) brandParts.push(`Brand/Channel: ${folderName}`);
if (ytChannel)  brandParts.push(`YouTube: ${ytChannel}`);
if (fbAccount)  brandParts.push(`Facebook: ${fbAccount}`);
if (ttAccount)  brandParts.push(`TikTok: ${ttAccount}`);
const brandContext = brandParts.length ? brandParts.join(". ") + ". " : "";
```

Both SEO endpoints now provide the AI with the full brand/channel context.

