The CORS configuration was missing `X-Requested-With` and `Accept` from `allowedHeaders`, and lacked an explicit `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials` response header — both required for proper browser cookie/session handling in credentialed cross-origin requests.

## Changes

- **`backend/src/app.js`**
  - Added `X-Requested-With` and `Accept` to the CORS `allowedHeaders` list
  - Added middleware to explicitly set `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` on every response

```js
app.use(cors({
  // ...
  allowedHeaders: ["Content-Type", "Authorization", "X-Requested-With", "Accept", "x-nextauth-secret"],
}));

app.use((req, res, next) => {
  res.header("Access-Control-Allow-Credentials", "true");
  next();
});
```

The dynamic origin allowlist, `PATCH` method, and `x-nextauth-secret` header are preserved.

