On initial page load, the "Total Users" stat briefly shows `0` before updating to the real count ~1 second later.

**Root cause:** `loadLeaderboard()` runs before `initAuth()` initialises `state.supabase`, so the first render falls back to empty `localStorage` and writes `0` to the stat element.

**Fix:** Guard the stat update in `renderLeaderboard` so it only writes when there are actual users:

```js
// before
if (statEl) statEl.textContent = String(totalUsers);

// after
if (statEl && totalUsers > 0) statEl.textContent = String(totalUsers);
```

The `—` placeholder is now preserved until real data arrives, eliminating the `0 → real count` flash.

